==========================================================================
STEP 2  Structural break detection (Section 3.1)
==========================================================================
PELT     :  11 breaks, 12 regimes (83.6s)
BP&ICSS  :   5 breaks (Bai-Perron 4, ICSS 1)

regimes seen in training : [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
regimes seen in testing  : [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11]
regimes that occur ONLY in the test window: [7, 8, 9, 10, 11]
Those one-hot columns are identically zero for every training row, so
the network cannot have learned a weight for them.  This is why the
paper's e_t encoding cannot generalise past the last training break.

